  "name": "Bashkir kurai and uzun-kyuy (Bashkir long song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The kurai, an end-blown flute traditionally cut from the stem of an umbellifer plant, is the national instrument of the Bashkirs of the southern Urals and is played with a drone hummed in the throat beneath the melody. Its core repertoire is the uzun-kyuy, slow, free-rhythm and heavily ornamented long songs on historical and lyrical subjects, alongside quicker dance tunes, and its 20th-century masters included Ishmulla Dilmukhametov and Gata Suleymanov. The sybyzgy card stands in for the kurai.",
  "recipe": "classic Eastern European early-1940s bashkir kurai and uzun-kyuy, drone Modal, wind pipe branch. many notes per syllable, solo unaccompanied, single lead single track no stacking. sybyzgy. moscow state label 1964-present major-flagship moscow melodiya studio. Neumann U47, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, Telefunken u73b broadcast comp, broadcast loudness EQ. tape 15ips hall reverb.",
